WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:03.949
Star Wars: The Last Jedi is a certified hit.

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:08.750
The film secured the second biggest domestic
opening weekend of all time, after only The

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.610
Force Awakens, and it earned a stellar 93%
rating on RottenTomatoes.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.309
From critics, that is.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:19.720
Audiences only gave it a 55%, with Star Wars
fans quickly taking sides.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.359
Sure, there are some things almost everyone
can agree on: the movie was beautiful to look

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:29.140
at, Adam Driver gave his best performance
yet as Kylo Ren, and the porgs weren't nearly

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.940
as annoying as some people feared.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.499
But there are still plenty of other things
to argue about.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:38.539
Here's a spoiler filled look at why audiences
are split on The Last Jedi.

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:40.319
Something old, something new

00:00:40.319 --> 00:00:44.329
While The Force Awakens was criticized for
basically being a retread of A New Hope, many

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:48.710
fans have praised The Last Jedi for being
something new in the Star Wars saga.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.769
One Twitter user wrote that the movie is "great
because it subverts any and all expectations

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:54.769
one could have.

00:00:54.769 --> 00:00:59.280
It goes places you wouldn't expect out of
a Disney Star Wars film, and proves that despite

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.929
most blockbusters feeling the exact same and
playing it safe, there can still be original

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.030
quality films."

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:10.250
Another said that they loved that everything
turned out "messy and unexpected" and added,

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.500
"It's brilliant about making you lose all
your mental bets about how things are about

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.619
to go."

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:16.799
And critics agree.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:21.960
Terri Schwartz of IGN wrote that there was
a scene that "is so stunning and unexpected

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.659
that I don't want to forget how I felt seeing
it for the first time," while Wired's Oliver

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:31.270
Franklin-Wallis said that while the film was
"imperfect," the unpredictability was "just

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.570
what Star Wars needs."

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:37.229
But some felt the film went too far, trying
way too hard to be different at the cost of

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.630
telling a good story.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.950
One Twitter user said, "The problem was that
it tried to be original but ended up being

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:48.859
an unoriginal mess with no real accomplishments,"
while a Rotten Tomatoes user argued that "instead

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:53.460
of building and enriching the things that
were set up in the previous movie, it DESTROYS

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.759
it and tries (unsuccessfully) to do its own
thing."

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:01.340
And others point out that for all its supposed
originality, The Last Jedi borrows heavily

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:07.600
from previous films, even swiping its entire
structure from The Empire Strikes Back.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.229
It's too long

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:14.940
Star Wars: The Last Jedi clocked in at 150
minutes, making it the longest film in the

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:20.000
franchise to date — 15 minutes longer than
2015's The Force Awakens, 17 minutes longer

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.739
than 2016's standalone Rogue One: A Star Wars
Story, and longer than other recent non-Star

00:02:25.739 --> 00:02:30.599
Wars blockbusters like The Avengers, Avengers:
Age of Ultron, and Captain America: Civil

00:02:30.599 --> 00:02:31.599
War.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.050
Even for a Star Wars fan, two and a half hours
in a theater — not including previews — is

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:40.660
a big commitment, and some felt the slow motion
chase scene through space in particular went

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.099
on for way too long.

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:47.260
"Anything you wanted to tell the audience
or the world about this one in comparison

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.330
to the other ones?"

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.819
"It's the longest one."

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:52.659
Freshmen hazing

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:57.170
One of the most impressive parts of The Force
Awakens was its ability to introduce and establish

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.569
a new, young, and diverse cast into the Star
Wars universe.

00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:06.040
The Last Jedi built on that by introducing
new characters like Rose, DJ, and Vice Admiral

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.040
Holdo.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.159
But while some fans loved these new additions,
especially praising the franchise's new commitment

00:03:11.159 --> 00:03:13.860
to diversity, not everyone was excited.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.260
One fan called them "forgettable," and another
said they were "useless."

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.659
Ouch.

00:03:19.659 --> 00:03:21.670
Middle child syndrome

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:24.870
Making the middle movie in a trilogy is a
difficult task.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.610
You don't have the benefit of taking time
to set up the characters, and you don't get

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.560
to resolve any dangling story threads.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.069
Some Last Jedi critics felt this narrative
stasis was the biggest issue with the film,

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:41.310
especially taking aim at Finn and Rose's side
mission to the casino city Canto Bight.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:45.230
It's also especially difficult for The Last
Jedi to be a middle chapter considering the

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:50.150
lofty expectations set up by the second film
in the original Star Wars trilogy, The Empire

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.629
Strikes Back — one of the most highly regarded
sequels of all time.

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:56.540
Living up to it was no easy task.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.349
A Jedi walks into a bar…

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:03.659
Star Wars has a history of blending the light
and dark, using its cheekier characters to

00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:06.290
introduce humor even in serious situations.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.830
And some people loved the many jokes in The
Last Jedi.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:13.909
However, some felt The Last Jedi went a little
too far, causing some fans to accuse the humor

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:15.640
of feeling forced.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:20.040
Some fans called out the film's opening scene,
in which Poe places a prank call to General

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.830
Hux as a distraction.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:26.610
Others had issues with Luke Skywalker milking
an alien for giggles, while one person said

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.060
he was given too many "cheesy" one-liners.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.720
Let's talk about Luke

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:35.670
The good news for fans of Luke Skywalker is
that this time around, he actually got to

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.010
say something.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.010
The bad news?

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.480
He dropped dead of apparent franchise fatigue
at the end of the movie.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:45.810
While most people agree that Hamill gave one
of his best performances, not everyone was

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:49.140
happy with the way Luke was portrayed — including
Hamill himself.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:55.190
"When I read 8, I told Rian, 'I fundamentally
disagree with virtually everything you've

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.990
decided about my character."

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:02.040
And many fans were upset at how Luke died,
peacefully disappearing into thin air instead

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.060
of going out in a blaze of glory.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:09.070
One Twitter user called it the "lamest death
ever" while another wrote that it was "honestly

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.490
insulting."

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.310
All your fan theories were wrong

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:16.560
After The Force Awakens planted a number of
clues about who Rey's parents are and who

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.330
Supreme Leader Snoke really is, fans spent
two years coming up with theories and debating

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:22.610
the possible answers.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.970
And then it turned out that — surprise!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.740
— none of that actually mattered at all.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.160
Some critics loved the way director Rian Johnson
threw all that back in everyone's faces in

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:35.940
order to just do his own thing, but many fans
were upset at getting no payoff for all the

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.600
expectations the franchise had previously
set up.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.630
A flubbed farewell?

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:45.840
Carrie Fisher's tragic death after completing
The Last Jedi made many of her moments in

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.090
the film as General Leia Organa even more
poignant for fans.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:53.570
Some fans, though, took issue with Leia's
use of the Force in the movie.

00:05:53.570 --> 00:05:58.430
The scene with the character floating through
space was cited by some as beautiful, showing

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:03.600
her character's resilience and finally answering
the long-held question of Leia's abilities.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.690
However, others felt it was cheesy and negated
what could have been a powerful moment for

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.690
the franchise.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:13.440
Johnson didn't change Leia's arc after Fisher's
death, and while Lucasfilm president Kathleen

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.400
Kennedy has said they won't use CGI to have
the character appear in Episode 9, the question

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.070
of her character's fate still remains unanswered.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:25.280
While no one could've predicted the real-life
circumstances the film had to deal with, losing

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.820
a character so central to the series is sure
to be difficult, and some felt The Last Jedi

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.850
sent her out on a mixed note.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:33.960
Thanks for watching!

